{
  "_readme": [
    "The live logger's pure state rules (spec 024, 028): how records order, how they split",
    "into sets, where the insertion cursor can stand and what position a new row gets,",
    "how offline ops re-anchor on replay, when an add collapses into an existing row, and",
    "how local and server search results merge. Two clients that disagree on any of this",
    "show two different logs for the same session.",
    "",
    "Records are plain objects: session_instance_tune_id, order_position, record_type",
    "('tune' | 'break'), deleted, tune_id, name, tune_type, and _temp on optimistic rows.",
    "IDs are integers for server rows and 'temp-<op_id>' strings for optimistic ones, so a",
    "port needs an id type that can be either. Several functions branch on which it is",
    "(seamActionFor only acts on integer ids; remapAnchors only rewrites 'temp-' strings).",
    "",
    "What a port must match exactly:",
    "  - order_position compares as plain JS strings: UTF-16 code-unit order. Positions",
    "    are ASCII base-62 (see fracindex.fixtures.json), so byte order agrees; never use",
    "    a locale-aware compare. A prefix sorts first ('a' < 'aV').",
    "  - computeOrdered's sort is STABLE: equal positions keep input order. In the app the",
    "    input is the record map's insertion order.",
    "  - maxPos scans every record, deleted and temp included, and ignores missing or null",
    "    positions. Its empty answer is '' (not null).",
    "  - Missing keys and null keys are different in remapAnchors: an anchor key that is",
    "    absent stays absent. record_ids arrays are NOT remapped — the callers keep temp",
    "    ids out of them (bulkDelete filters temps), and a port must keep that invariant.",
    "  - normName: fold smart single quotes (U+2018 U+2019 U+201B U+02BC U+2032 ` U+00B4)",
    "    to ', smart doubles (U+201C U+201D U+201E U+2033 U+00AB U+00BB) to \", then NFD",
    "    and delete U+0300-U+036F, then JS trim (Unicode whitespace incl. U+00A0), then",
    "    JS toLowerCase. NFD, not NFKD: ligatures like U+FB01 survive. It does NOT drop",
    "    'the'; stripThe does, and only a lowercase 'the' followed by whitespace.",
    "  - pluralType adds 'es' after s, z, ch, sh or x (case-insensitive), else 's'. It",
    "    does not know about already-plural input ('Slides' -> 'Slideses').",
    "  - setLabel compares tune types case-sensitively ('Reel' and 'reel' are Mixed) and",
    "    ignores null and ''.",
    "  - mergeStable caps at 8 rows. An enriched row takes the server's in_session_tune",
    "    EVEN WHEN the server row has none (the key then disappears), and the server's abc",
    "    unless that is null/absent. Server rows with a null tune_id are dropped. See the",
    "    notes on the cases that pin the odd parts.",
    "  - Cursor values: null = the end, <id> = after that tune, {\"before\": id} = the start",
    "    of that tune's set, {\"newSet\": id} = a new set in the gap before that tune.",
    "  - nextTs is fixtured with a scripted clock (harness 'clock'): each case starts from a",
    "    fresh counter at 0; input.clock[i] is Date.now() at call i and expected[i] is what",
    "    call i returns. The rule is max(clock, last + 1).",
    "",
    "parseThesessionId / parseThesessionSettingId are re-exports of shared/parse.js,",
    "fixtured here because the logger's paste detection depends on them. The domain match",
    "is case-sensitive, and parseInt drops leading zeros."
  ],

  "_not_fixtured": {
    "normAbc": "re-export of shared/abcquery.js normAbc; fixtured in shared/abcquery.fixtures.json"
  },

  "functions": {
    "nextTs": {
      "params": [],
      "harness": "clock",
      "cases": [
        { "name": "follows the wall clock when it is ahead", "input": { "clock": [3000000] }, "expected": [3000000] },
        { "name": "strictly increasing within a frozen millisecond", "input": { "clock": [1000000, 1000000, 1000000] }, "expected": [1000000, 1000001, 1000002] },
        { "name": "monotonic when the clock steps backwards", "input": { "clock": [2000000, 1500000] }, "expected": [2000000, 2000001] },
        { "name": "catches back up to the clock", "input": { "clock": [100, 100, 101, 200] }, "expected": [100, 101, 102, 200] },
        { "name": "a zero clock still starts at 1", "input": { "clock": [0, 0] }, "expected": [1, 2] }
      ]
    },

    "computeOrdered": {
      "params": ["records"],
      "cases": [
        {
          "name": "drops deleted rows and sorts by position",
          "input": {
            "records": [
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 3, "order_position": "C", "record_type": "tune", "deleted": false },
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "order_position": "A", "record_type": "tune", "deleted": false },
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "order_position": "B", "record_type": "tune", "deleted": true },
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 4, "order_position": "D", "record_type": "break", "deleted": false }
            ]
          },
          "expected": [
            { "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "order_position": "A", "record_type": "tune", "deleted": false },
            { "session_instance_tune_id": 3, "order_position": "C", "record_type": "tune", "deleted": false },
            { "session_instance_tune_id": 4, "order_position": "D", "record_type": "break", "deleted": false }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "byte order: digits < upper < lower, and a prefix sorts first",
          "input": {
            "records": [
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "order_position": "aV" },
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "order_position": "a" },
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 3, "order_position": "Z" },
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 4, "order_position": "9" },
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 5, "order_position": "VV" },
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 6, "order_position": "V" }
            ]
          },
          "expected": [
            { "session_instance_tune_id": 4, "order_position": "9" },
            { "session_instance_tune_id": 6, "order_position": "V" },
            { "session_instance_tune_id": 5, "order_position": "VV" },
            { "session_instance_tune_id": 3, "order_position": "Z" },
            { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "order_position": "a" },
            { "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "order_position": "aV" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "equal positions keep input order (stable sort)",
          "input": {
            "records": [
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 9, "order_position": "V" },
              { "session_instance_tune_id": "temp-x", "order_position": "V", "_temp": true },
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "order_position": "V" },
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "order_position": "F" }
            ]
          },
          "expected": [
            { "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "order_position": "F" },
            { "session_instance_tune_id": 9, "order_position": "V" },
            { "session_instance_tune_id": "temp-x", "order_position": "V", "_temp": true },
            { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "order_position": "V" }
          ]
        },
        { "name": "empty", "input": { "records": [] }, "expected": [] }
      ]
    },

    "segmentByBreaks": {
      "params": ["ordered"],
      "cases": [
        {
          "name": "splits on breaks; each set remembers the break that ends it; the open set has null",
          "input": {
            "ordered": [
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "record_type": "tune" },
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "record_type": "tune" },
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 3, "record_type": "break" },
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 4, "record_type": "tune" }
            ]
          },
          "expected": [
            { "tunes": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "record_type": "tune" }, { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "record_type": "tune" }], "breakAfter": 3 },
            { "tunes": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 4, "record_type": "tune" }], "breakAfter": null }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "a leading break is ignored; a trailing break closes the last set",
          "input": {
            "ordered": [
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "record_type": "break" },
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "record_type": "tune" },
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 3, "record_type": "break" }
            ]
          },
          "expected": [{ "tunes": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "record_type": "tune" }], "breakAfter": 3 }]
        },
        {
          "name": "consecutive breaks: only the first one closes the set",
          "input": {
            "ordered": [
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "record_type": "tune" },
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "record_type": "break" },
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 3, "record_type": "break" },
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 4, "record_type": "tune" }
            ]
          },
          "expected": [
            { "tunes": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "record_type": "tune" }], "breakAfter": 2 },
            { "tunes": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 4, "record_type": "tune" }], "breakAfter": null }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "anything that is not a break counts as a tune",
          "input": { "ordered": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 1 }] },
          "expected": [{ "tunes": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 1 }], "breakAfter": null }]
        },
        {
          "name": "only breaks: no sets",
          "input": { "ordered": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "record_type": "break" }] },
          "expected": []
        },
        { "name": "empty", "input": { "ordered": [] }, "expected": [] }
      ]
    },

    "setsOf": {
      "params": ["segments"],
      "cases": [
        {
          "name": "the tune lists of each segment",
          "input": {
            "segments": [
              { "tunes": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 1 }], "breakAfter": 2 },
              { "tunes": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 3 }], "breakAfter": null }
            ]
          },
          "expected": [[{ "session_instance_tune_id": 1 }], [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 3 }]]
        },
        { "name": "empty", "input": { "segments": [] }, "expected": [] }
      ]
    },

    "tunesOf": {
      "params": ["ordered"],
      "cases": [
        {
          "name": "drops breaks, keeps order",
          "input": {
            "ordered": [
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "record_type": "tune" },
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "record_type": "break" },
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 3 }
            ]
          },
          "expected": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "record_type": "tune" }, { "session_instance_tune_id": 3 }]
        }
      ]
    },

    "pluralType": {
      "params": ["ty"],
      "cases": [
        { "name": "Reel", "input": { "ty": "Reel" }, "expected": "Reels" },
        { "name": "lowercase reel", "input": { "ty": "reel" }, "expected": "reels" },
        { "name": "Slip Jig", "input": { "ty": "Slip Jig" }, "expected": "Slip Jigs" },
        { "name": "Hornpipe", "input": { "ty": "Hornpipe" }, "expected": "Hornpipes" },
        { "name": "Barndance", "input": { "ty": "Barndance" }, "expected": "Barndances" },
        { "name": "Strathspey", "input": { "ty": "Strathspey" }, "expected": "Strathspeys" },
        { "name": "Three-Two", "input": { "ty": "Three-Two" }, "expected": "Three-Twos" },
        { "name": "z takes es", "input": { "ty": "Waltz" }, "expected": "Waltzes" },
        { "name": "ch takes es", "input": { "ty": "March" }, "expected": "Marches" },
        { "name": "sh takes es", "input": { "ty": "Flash" }, "expected": "Flashes" },
        { "name": "x takes es", "input": { "ty": "Box" }, "expected": "Boxes" },
        { "name": "case-insensitive ending", "input": { "ty": "MARCH" }, "expected": "MARCHes" },
        { "name": "already plural is not detected", "input": { "ty": "Slides" }, "expected": "Slideses", "note": "Only reachable if a tune_type were stored plural; thesession types are singular." },
        { "name": "empty string passes through", "input": { "ty": "" }, "expected": "" },
        { "name": "null passes through", "input": { "ty": null }, "expected": null }
      ]
    },

    "setLabel": {
      "params": ["setTunes"],
      "cases": [
        { "name": "shared type, pluralized", "input": { "setTunes": [{ "tune_type": "Reel" }, { "tune_type": "Reel" }] }, "expected": "Reels" },
        { "name": "two types are Mixed", "input": { "setTunes": [{ "tune_type": "Reel" }, { "tune_type": "Jig" }] }, "expected": "Mixed" },
        { "name": "case differs: Mixed", "input": { "setTunes": [{ "tune_type": "Reel" }, { "tune_type": "reel" }] }, "expected": "Mixed" },
        { "name": "unmatched tunes do not make it Mixed", "input": { "setTunes": [{ "tune_type": null }, { "tune_type": "" }, { "tune_type": "Jig" }, {}] }, "expected": "Jigs" },
        { "name": "no matched tune: Unknown", "input": { "setTunes": [{ "tune_type": null }] }, "expected": "Unknown" },
        { "name": "empty set: Unknown", "input": { "setTunes": [] }, "expected": "Unknown" }
      ]
    },

    "maxPos": {
      "params": ["records"],
      "cases": [
        {
          "name": "scans deleted and temp rows too",
          "input": {
            "records": [
              { "order_position": "A" },
              { "order_position": "Z", "deleted": true },
              { "order_position": "M", "_temp": true }
            ]
          },
          "expected": "Z"
        },
        { "name": "lowercase beats uppercase; missing and null are skipped", "input": { "records": [{ "order_position": null }, { "order_position": "a" }, { "order_position": "Z" }, {}] }, "expected": "a" },
        { "name": "a longer key with the same prefix wins", "input": { "records": [{ "order_position": "z" }, { "order_position": "zV" }] }, "expected": "zV" },
        { "name": "empty is the empty string", "input": { "records": [] }, "expected": "" }
      ]
    },

    "cursorPos": {
      "params": ["insertAfterId", "ordered", "allRecords"],
      "cases": [
        {
          "name": "null cursor appends past the high-water mark",
          "input": {
            "insertAfterId": null,
            "ordered": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "order_position": "A" }, { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "order_position": "C" }],
            "allRecords": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "order_position": "A" }, { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "order_position": "C" }]
          },
          "expected": { "afterId": null, "beforeId": null, "position": "D" }
        },
        {
          "name": "append uses ALL records, including deleted ones",
          "input": {
            "insertAfterId": null,
            "ordered": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "order_position": "A" }, { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "order_position": "C" }],
            "allRecords": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "order_position": "A" }, { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "order_position": "C" }, { "session_instance_tune_id": 3, "order_position": "z", "deleted": true }]
          },
          "expected": { "afterId": null, "beforeId": null, "position": "zV" }
        },
        {
          "name": "append to an empty log starts at V",
          "input": { "insertAfterId": null, "ordered": [], "allRecords": [] },
          "expected": { "afterId": null, "beforeId": null, "position": "V" }
        },
        {
          "name": "after a tune: between it and the next",
          "input": {
            "insertAfterId": 1,
            "ordered": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "order_position": "A" }, { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "order_position": "C" }],
            "allRecords": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "order_position": "A" }, { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "order_position": "C" }]
          },
          "expected": { "afterId": 1, "beforeId": null, "position": "B" }
        },
        {
          "name": "after the last tune: append past it, anchored",
          "input": {
            "insertAfterId": 2,
            "ordered": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "order_position": "A" }, { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "order_position": "C" }],
            "allRecords": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "order_position": "A" }, { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "order_position": "C" }]
          },
          "expected": { "afterId": 2, "beforeId": null, "position": "D" }
        },
        {
          "name": "before the first tune",
          "input": {
            "insertAfterId": { "before": 1 },
            "ordered": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "order_position": "A" }, { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "order_position": "C" }],
            "allRecords": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "order_position": "A" }, { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "order_position": "C" }]
          },
          "expected": { "afterId": null, "beforeId": 1, "position": "5" }
        },
        {
          "name": "before a later tune: between it and its predecessor",
          "input": {
            "insertAfterId": { "before": 2 },
            "ordered": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "order_position": "A" }, { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "order_position": "C" }],
            "allRecords": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "order_position": "A" }, { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "order_position": "C" }]
          },
          "expected": { "afterId": null, "beforeId": 2, "position": "B" }
        },
        {
          "name": "adjacent neighbours extend the key",
          "input": {
            "insertAfterId": 1,
            "ordered": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "order_position": "V" }, { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "order_position": "W" }],
            "allRecords": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "order_position": "V" }, { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "order_position": "W" }]
          },
          "expected": { "afterId": 1, "beforeId": null, "position": "VV" }
        },
        {
          "name": "a temp id anchor works like any other",
          "input": {
            "insertAfterId": "temp-a",
            "ordered": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": "temp-a", "order_position": "V", "_temp": true }, { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "order_position": "X" }],
            "allRecords": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": "temp-a", "order_position": "V", "_temp": true }, { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "order_position": "X" }]
          },
          "expected": { "afterId": "temp-a", "beforeId": null, "position": "W" }
        },
        {
          "name": "a vanished after-anchor degrades to append",
          "input": {
            "insertAfterId": 999,
            "ordered": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "order_position": "A" }, { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "order_position": "C" }],
            "allRecords": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "order_position": "A" }, { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "order_position": "C" }]
          },
          "expected": { "afterId": null, "beforeId": null, "position": "D" }
        },
        {
          "name": "a vanished before-anchor degrades to append",
          "input": {
            "insertAfterId": { "before": 999 },
            "ordered": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "order_position": "A" }, { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "order_position": "C" }],
            "allRecords": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "order_position": "A" }, { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "order_position": "C" }]
          },
          "expected": { "afterId": null, "beforeId": null, "position": "D" }
        },
        {
          "name": "a newSet cursor is not a position: append",
          "input": {
            "insertAfterId": { "newSet": 2 },
            "ordered": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "order_position": "A" }, { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "order_position": "C" }],
            "allRecords": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "order_position": "A" }, { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "order_position": "C" }]
          },
          "expected": { "afterId": null, "beforeId": null, "position": "D" },
          "note": "The App handles {newSet} itself (add + set_break before the next set) and never passes it here. Pinned so a port does not invent a meaning for it."
        }
      ]
    },

    "remapAnchors": {
      "params": ["payload", "tempToReal"],
      "mapParams": ["tempToReal"],
      "cases": [
        {
          "name": "rewrites temp after/before anchors",
          "input": { "payload": { "after_record_id": "temp-a", "before_record_id": "temp-b", "tune_id": 5 }, "tempToReal": [["temp-a", 100], ["temp-b", 200]] },
          "expected": { "payload": { "after_record_id": 100, "before_record_id": 200, "tune_id": 5 }, "skip": false }
        },
        {
          "name": "an unresolved anchor falls back to null (append)",
          "input": { "payload": { "after_record_id": "temp-unknown" }, "tempToReal": [["temp-a", 100]] },
          "expected": { "payload": { "after_record_id": null }, "skip": false }
        },
        {
          "name": "real anchors and null anchors are untouched",
          "input": { "payload": { "after_record_id": 55, "before_record_id": null }, "tempToReal": [["temp-a", 100]] },
          "expected": { "payload": { "after_record_id": 55, "before_record_id": null }, "skip": false }
        },
        {
          "name": "absent anchor keys stay absent",
          "input": { "payload": { "action": "insert" }, "tempToReal": [] },
          "expected": { "payload": { "action": "insert" }, "skip": false }
        },
        {
          "name": "only the 'temp-' prefix marks a temp id",
          "input": { "payload": { "after_record_id": "tempo" }, "tempToReal": [["tempo", 1]] },
          "expected": { "payload": { "after_record_id": "tempo" }, "skip": false }
        },
        {
          "name": "a temp record_id target resolves",
          "input": { "payload": { "record_id": "temp-a", "confidence": 100 }, "tempToReal": [["temp-a", 100]] },
          "expected": { "payload": { "record_id": 100, "confidence": 100 }, "skip": false }
        },
        {
          "name": "a temp record_id that resolves to 0 is still resolved",
          "input": { "payload": { "record_id": "temp-a" }, "tempToReal": [["temp-a", 0]] },
          "expected": { "payload": { "record_id": 0 }, "skip": false }
        },
        {
          "name": "an unresolved temp record_id skips the op (anchors still remapped)",
          "input": { "payload": { "record_id": "temp-orphan", "after_record_id": "temp-a" }, "tempToReal": [["temp-a", 100]] },
          "expected": { "payload": { "record_id": "temp-orphan", "after_record_id": 100 }, "skip": true }
        },
        {
          "name": "a null record_id is not a skip",
          "input": { "payload": { "record_id": null }, "tempToReal": [] },
          "expected": { "payload": { "record_id": null }, "skip": false }
        },
        {
          "name": "record_ids arrays are not remapped",
          "input": { "payload": { "record_ids": ["temp-a", 5] }, "tempToReal": [["temp-a", 100]] },
          "expected": { "payload": { "record_ids": ["temp-a", 5] }, "skip": false },
          "note": "Callers keep temp ids out of record_ids (bulkDelete filters _temp rows), so this is unreachable today. A port must keep that invariant or remap here."
        }
      ]
    },

    "stripThe": {
      "params": ["s"],
      "cases": [
        { "name": "drops a leading lowercase the", "input": { "s": "the silver spear" }, "expected": "silver spear" },
        { "name": "any whitespace run after it", "input": { "s": "the  kesh" }, "expected": "kesh" },
        { "name": "case-sensitive: The is kept", "input": { "s": "The Kesh" }, "expected": "The Kesh" },
        { "name": "whole word only", "input": { "s": "theatre" }, "expected": "theatre" },
        { "name": "bare the is kept", "input": { "s": "the" }, "expected": "the" },
        { "name": "no the", "input": { "s": "silver spear" }, "expected": "silver spear" }
      ]
    },

    "normName": {
      "params": ["s"],
      "cases": [
        { "name": "folds U+2019, trims, lowercases", "input": { "s": "  Cooley’s  " }, "expected": "cooley's" },
        { "name": "folds U+02BC", "input": { "s": "Cooleyʼs" }, "expected": "cooley's" },
        { "name": "folds U+2032 prime", "input": { "s": "Cooley′s" }, "expected": "cooley's" },
        { "name": "folds smart doubles", "input": { "s": "“X” «Y»" }, "expected": "\"x\" \"y\"" },
        { "name": "strips diacritics", "input": { "s": "Sligo Maíd" }, "expected": "sligo maid" },
        { "name": "strips diacritics from capitals", "input": { "s": "ÉIRINN" }, "expected": "eirinn" },
        { "name": "keeps the article", "input": { "s": "The Silver Spear" }, "expected": "the silver spear" },
        { "name": "trims non-breaking spaces", "input": { "s": " The Kesh " }, "expected": "the kesh" },
        { "name": "NFD, not NFKD: a ligature survives", "input": { "s": "ﬁddle" }, "expected": "ﬁddle" },
        { "name": "eszett is not expanded", "input": { "s": "Straße" }, "expected": "straße" },
        { "name": "null", "input": { "s": null }, "expected": "" },
        { "name": "empty", "input": { "s": "" }, "expected": "" }
      ]
    },

    "openSetMergeTarget": {
      "params": ["payload", "ordered"],
      "cases": [
        {
          "name": "linked: same tune_id in the open set",
          "input": {
            "payload": { "tune_id": 9 },
            "ordered": [
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "record_type": "tune", "tune_id": 7 },
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "record_type": "tune", "tune_id": 9 }
            ]
          },
          "expected": { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "record_type": "tune", "tune_id": 9 }
        },
        {
          "name": "linked: the first match wins",
          "input": {
            "payload": { "tune_id": 5 },
            "ordered": [
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "record_type": "tune", "tune_id": 5, "name": "Kesh" },
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "record_type": "tune", "tune_id": 5 }
            ]
          },
          "expected": { "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "record_type": "tune", "tune_id": 5, "name": "Kesh" }
        },
        {
          "name": "unlinked: identical normalized name on an unlinked row",
          "input": {
            "payload": { "name": "cooley's" },
            "ordered": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "record_type": "tune", "tune_id": null, "name": "Cooley’s" }]
          },
          "expected": { "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "record_type": "tune", "tune_id": null, "name": "Cooley’s" }
        },
        {
          "name": "unlinked add never merges into a LINKED row, even by name",
          "input": {
            "payload": { "name": "kesh" },
            "ordered": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "record_type": "tune", "tune_id": 5, "name": "Kesh" }]
          },
          "expected": null
        },
        {
          "name": "unlinked: names must match exactly after normName (the article counts)",
          "input": {
            "payload": { "name": "the kesh" },
            "ordered": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "record_type": "tune", "tune_id": null, "name": "Kesh" }]
          },
          "expected": null
        },
        {
          "name": "unlinked with an empty name matches nothing",
          "input": {
            "payload": { "tune_id": null, "name": "" },
            "ordered": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "record_type": "tune", "tune_id": null, "name": "" }]
          },
          "expected": null
        },
        {
          "name": "a duplicate in a CLOSED set does not count",
          "input": {
            "payload": { "tune_id": 7 },
            "ordered": [
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "record_type": "tune", "tune_id": 7 },
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "record_type": "break" },
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 3, "record_type": "tune", "tune_id": 9 }
            ]
          },
          "expected": null
        },
        {
          "name": "a trailing break leaves an empty open set",
          "input": {
            "payload": { "tune_id": 7 },
            "ordered": [
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "record_type": "tune", "tune_id": 7 },
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "record_type": "break" }
            ]
          },
          "expected": null
        },
        {
          "name": "only the LAST break opens the set",
          "input": {
            "payload": { "tune_id": 7 },
            "ordered": [
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "record_type": "break" },
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "record_type": "tune", "tune_id": 7 },
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 3, "record_type": "break" },
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 4, "record_type": "tune", "tune_id": 7 }
            ]
          },
          "expected": { "session_instance_tune_id": 4, "record_type": "tune", "tune_id": 7 }
        },
        {
          "name": "temp and deleted rows are skipped",
          "input": {
            "payload": { "tune_id": 7 },
            "ordered": [
              { "session_instance_tune_id": "temp-a", "record_type": "tune", "tune_id": 7, "_temp": true },
              { "session_instance_tune_id": 2, "record_type": "tune", "tune_id": 7, "deleted": true }
            ]
          },
          "expected": null
        },
        {
          "name": "a row without record_type 'tune' is skipped",
          "input": {
            "payload": { "tune_id": 7 },
            "ordered": [{ "session_instance_tune_id": 1, "tune_id": 7 }]
          },
          "expected": null
        },
        { "name": "empty log", "input": { "payload": { "tune_id": 7 }, "ordered": [] }, "expected": null }
      ]
    },

    "mergeStable": {
      "params": ["localList", "serverList"],
      "cases": [
        {
          "name": "local rows stay pinned and are enriched; server-only rows append",
          "input": {
            "localList": [{ "tune_id": 1, "name": "A" }, { "tune_id": 2, "name": "B" }],
            "serverList": [{ "tune_id": 2, "name": "B", "in_session_tune": true, "abc": "xyz" }, { "tune_id": 3, "name": "C" }]
          },
          "expected": [
            { "tune_id": 1, "name": "A" },
            { "tune_id": 2, "name": "B", "in_session_tune": true, "abc": "xyz" },
            { "tune_id": 3, "name": "C" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "enrichment copies only in_session_tune and abc, not the server's name",
          "input": {
            "localList": [{ "tune_id": 1, "name": "Local Name" }],
            "serverList": [{ "tune_id": 1, "name": "Server Name", "tune_type": "Reel", "in_session_tune": false }]
          },
          "expected": [{ "tune_id": 1, "name": "Local Name", "in_session_tune": false }]
        },
        {
          "name": "a null server abc keeps the local abc",
          "input": {
            "localList": [{ "tune_id": 1, "name": "A", "abc": "loc" }],
            "serverList": [{ "tune_id": 1, "name": "A", "abc": null, "in_session_tune": false }]
          },
          "expected": [{ "tune_id": 1, "name": "A", "abc": "loc", "in_session_tune": false }]
        },
        {
          "name": "a server row with no in_session_tune CLEARS the local one",
          "input": {
            "localList": [{ "tune_id": 1, "name": "A", "in_session_tune": true, "abc": "loc" }],
            "serverList": [{ "tune_id": 1, "name": "A" }]
          },
          "expected": [{ "tune_id": 1, "name": "A", "abc": "loc" }],
          "note": "Looks unintended: the spread sets in_session_tune to undefined. Harmless while the server always sends the field."
        },
        {
          "name": "server rows with a null tune_id are dropped",
          "input": {
            "localList": [{ "tune_id": null, "name": "unlinked" }],
            "serverList": [{ "tune_id": null, "name": "v" }]
          },
          "expected": [{ "tune_id": null, "name": "unlinked" }]
        },
        {
          "name": "duplicate server-only rows are both appended",
          "input": {
            "localList": [],
            "serverList": [{ "tune_id": 3 }, { "tune_id": 3, "name": "dup" }]
          },
          "expected": [{ "tune_id": 3 }, { "tune_id": 3, "name": "dup" }],
          "note": "Not deduplicated. The server does not send duplicates, so this is unreachable today."
        },
        {
          "name": "duplicate server rows: the LAST one enriches a local row",
          "input": {
            "localList": [{ "tune_id": 3, "name": "L" }],
            "serverList": [{ "tune_id": 3, "in_session_tune": true }, { "tune_id": 3, "in_session_tune": false }]
          },
          "expected": [{ "tune_id": 3, "name": "L", "in_session_tune": false }]
        },
        {
          "name": "never more than 8 rows; local rows first",
          "input": {
            "localList": [{ "tune_id": 1 }, { "tune_id": 2 }, { "tune_id": 3 }, { "tune_id": 4 }, { "tune_id": 5 }, { "tune_id": 6 }],
            "serverList": [{ "tune_id": 100 }, { "tune_id": 101 }, { "tune_id": 102 }, { "tune_id": 103 }]
          },
          "expected": [{ "tune_id": 1 }, { "tune_id": 2 }, { "tune_id": 3 }, { "tune_id": 4 }, { "tune_id": 5 }, { "tune_id": 6 }, { "tune_id": 100 }, { "tune_id": 101 }]
        },
        {
          "name": "more than 8 local rows are cut too",
          "input": {
            "localList": [{ "tune_id": 1 }, { "tune_id": 2 }, { "tune_id": 3 }, { "tune_id": 4 }, { "tune_id": 5 }, { "tune_id": 6 }, { "tune_id": 7 }, { "tune_id": 8 }, { "tune_id": 9 }],
            "serverList": []
          },
          "expected": [{ "tune_id": 1 }, { "tune_id": 2 }, { "tune_id": 3 }, { "tune_id": 4 }, { "tune_id": 5 }, { "tune_id": 6 }, { "tune_id": 7 }, { "tune_id": 8 }]
        },
        { "name": "both empty", "input": { "localList": [], "serverList": [] }, "expected": [] }
      ]
    },

    "parseThesessionId": {
